                <h2>Pre-Recharge Preparation for New Accounts</h2>
<p>When opening Meta, Google, or TikTok ad accounts, teams often focus on creatives and bidding while overlooking financial standardization. Complete this checklist immediately after account setup to avoid reconciliation chaos later.</p>
<p><strong>Recharge Information Registration:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Record each account's Account ID/BM ID, mapped to internal project codes</li>
<li>[ ] Create an account balance ledger; register date, amount, and currency immediately upon recharge confirmation</li>
<li>[ ] Confirm the recharge method: direct recharge, monthly billing, or agency transfer—different methods affect invoice headers</li>
<li>[ ] Save recharge receipts/screenshots and archive them for reference</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Common Issue:</strong> A utility app team managing 3 regional accounts mixed up balance allocations, making monthly cost attribution impossible. Register accounts separately by region and project from the start.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Three Key Monitoring Points for Daily Spend Tracking</h2>
<p>Overseas ad platforms have data delays and varying display logic. Operations staff need correct monitoring methods for accurate data.</p>
<p><strong>Daily Checklist (recommended: 4 PM daily):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Log into each platform dashboard and record total daily spend</li>
<li>[ ] Check if any account balance falls below the warning threshold (recommend 20% of daily spend as alert line)</li>
<li>[ ] Log abnormal spend fluctuations: single-day spend changes exceeding 30% require investigation</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Weekly Review:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Aggregate weekly spend data across all accounts; compare against budget</li>
<li>[ ] Verify pending charges (some platforms have 24-48 hour delays)</li>
<li>[ ] Confirm if weekly recharges are fully consumed and if balances are sufficient</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Month-End Cutoff:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Capture month-end spend snapshots for all accounts</li>
<li>[ ] Distinguish between billed spend and estimated spend (some platforms show preliminary values)</li>
<li>[ ] Freeze current month financial data as reconciliation baseline</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Standardized Monthly Invoice Verification Process</h2>
<p>Invoices are core financial documents, but overseas ad platform invoice rules vary widely. Execute this process monthly.</p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Invoice Application</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Platform</th>
<th>Invoice Access Path</th>
<th>Application Timing</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta Business</td>
<td>Billing Center &gt; Invoices &gt; Download</td>
<td>Available after 5th of following month</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google Ads</td>
<td>Tools &gt; Billing &gt; Invoices</td>
<td>Available after 3rd of following month</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok Ads</td>
<td>Reports &gt; Billing &gt; Request Invoice</td>
<td>Submit before 10th of following month</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Step 2: Information Verification</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Match invoice amount to platform billing statement (allow ±2% exchange rate variance)</li>
<li>[ ] Verify invoice header, tax ID, and bank details are correct</li>
<li>[ ] Confirm invoice account numbers match registered ledger entries</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 3: Internal Reconciliation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Upload scanned invoice to financial system</li>
<li>[ ] Link to corresponding project advertising cost records</li>
<li>[ ] Complete cost allocation and confirm ROI calculation basis</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Three-Way Verification Checklist: Recharge-Spend-Invoice</h2>
<p>After completing the above steps, use this checklist for final verification:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Total Recharge = Consumed Amount + Account Balance (refunds require separate line items)</li>
<li>[ ] Invoice Total = Sum of all account monthly spend (verify no accounts are missing)</li>
<li>[ ] Reconciliation variance exceeding 5% requires documented explanation with operations and finance sign-off</li>
<li>[ ] Maintain reconciliation cycle log and archive monthly</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Practical Tip:</strong> A cross-border e-commerce team discovered invoices were 8% less than actual spend throughout the year. Investigation revealed agency-issued invoices for certain country sites were not being transmitted promptly. Include invoice transmission deadlines in agency contracts and set reminders.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Quick Reference: Troubleshooting Common Issues</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Situation</th>
<th>Solution</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Account shows overdue despite sufficient balance</td>
<td>Check for pending refunds or Credits</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Invoice amount less than platform bill</td>
<td>Platform may have pre-deducted taxes; actual received amount follows invoice</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Month-end recharge unspent</td>
<td>Balance rolls over to next month; no additional action needed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Invoice portal inaccessible</td>
<td>Verify account status; invoices unavailable for overdue accounts</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<p><strong>Core Principle:</strong> Overseas ad reconciliation has no universal standard—each platform operates differently. Teams must establish recharge-spend-invoice ledger templates at project launch and assign dedicated staff for daily maintenance. Once the workflow is established, monthly financial reconciliation efficiency improves by 50% or more.</p>
